This directory vendors the Vue grammar from:

    tree-sitter-vue-updated 0.1.0
    (generated from https://github.com/c-gamble/tree-sitter-vue)
    License: MIT

The only modification from upstream is in src/tree_sitter_html/scanner.cc: the five
exported functions

    tree_sitter_html_external_scanner_{create,destroy,scan,serialize,deserialize}

are renamed to tree_sitter_vue_vendored_html_external_scanner_*. They are dead code
in this grammar (the Vue scanner in src/scanner.cc uses the bundled `Scanner` class
directly and never calls them), but as exported symbols they collided at link time
with the identically named functions in the tree-sitter-html crate, silently
breaking ripple's HTML adapter. Renaming them removes the collision with no change in
behavior. See ripple issue #48.

